&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Cards team at Stripe is responsible for the infrastructure, user-facing features, and business of accepting credit, debit, and prepaid card payments. Delivering the best offering for processing credit, debit, and prepaid cards is critical to Stripe’s mission, given the central role card payments play in internet commerce.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a product manager to drive our card network efforts and strategy across Europe and Asia Pacific. Specifically, this product manager will own the products and infrastructure powering our processing for local and regional card networks, including domestic card schemes and co-badged cards. A world-class card processing offering is the foundation on which our business is built and what our customers continuously expect. As a result, it is critical that we continuously expand, improve, and maintain the edge of our card processing capabilities. We believe Stripe can truly succeed here and are searching for the right product manager to lead this product effort.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is an opportunity to truly “own” a critical platform within Stripe’s core business. This product manager will partner with experienced engineering leads to define and deliver the associated product and infrastructure for these efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with go-to-market teams (Sales and Account Management) to define how to expand or improve our coverage of local and regional card networks to meet the needs of our customers in Europe and Asia Pacific&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Business Development and Partnerships to represent our product and users in negotiations with local and regional card networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with merchants to understand their current experience accepting local and regional card brands, associated pain points, and opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Engineering to develop Stripe’s roadmap for local and regional card networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Finance to understand the costs of processing across Stripe’s local and regional card networks and drive improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product experience: 6 to 10 years of relevant experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business acumen and data-driven problem-solving: You enjoy digging into the details of how a business works, identifying how to make it better, and building product and technical solutions to do so. You dig deep into the data, think from first principles, and deliver the right results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer- and partner-facing experience: You’re comfortable in front of customers or third-party collaborators and have experience navigating customer conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational execution: You are strong operationally, capable of structuring and leading a cross-functional team and designing and driving processes. You enjoy doing whatever it takes to execute on complex projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication: You pay close attention to detail and communicate precisely and effectively, including with external customers and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL or a willingness and aptitude to learn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in an external-facing role (sales or partnerships) and in business negotiations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building ML-based products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Financial Systems organization builds the technology that enables Stripe’s Finance org to operate accurately, efficiently, and at Stripe’s scale. We develop trusted data products, internal platforms and products, and intelligent workflows that help Finance teams manage complex global operations while maintaining strong controls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will join a product team focused on transforming finance operations. You will initially work closely with Stripe’s tax and treasury organizations with opportunities for future impact in other parts of the Finance org. The products you build will help experts find trusted information, coordinate work, identify exceptions, and make timely decisions without stitching together context and workflows across multiple systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will develop products that will enable Stripe to maintain a continuously updated understanding of financial performance, automate complex operations while maintaining rigorous financial controls that minimize risk, and reduce toil for domain experts to free them for higher-value work. You will develop a deep understanding of expert users and their workflows, own the product strategy, turn it into a focused roadmap, and lead products from discovery through adoption and continuous improvement. The transformation your products enable will reduce risk, improve efficiency, automate manual tasks, and better enable Stripe to make timely financial decisions, deliver on regulatory commitments, and run a global-scale business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role combines internal product development, data platforms, automated workflow design, and applied AI. You will help develop purpose-built solutions, platforms, and autonomous agentic capabilities that reason over governed data, drive end-to-end workflows, and support expert decisions. Success requires understanding the capabilities and limitations of AI and machine learning when applied to business-critical, regulated, and strictly governed problems. You will also use AI-enabled tools throughout the product development lifecycle to accelerate discovery, prototyping, requirements development, evaluation, and iteration without compromising quality or controls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of Finance users, jobs-to-be-done, compliance and regulatory considerations, and data dependencies, then translate that understanding into a clear roadmap for agentic automations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own products end to end, from problem discovery and strategy through delivery, adoption, measurement, and iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reusable data and self-serve workflow capabilities that eliminate manual overhead and enable future automated Finance use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance, engineering, data, security, legal, and others to make sound product and architecture tradeoffs in a business-critical and control-sensitive environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define measures to understand adoption, engagement, and impact for products and develop insights into the metrics to guide improvements to the product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop Finance products that enable Stripes to self-serve the creation and operation of agentic automations, while establishing appropriate boundaries for autonomous execution, evaluation methods, and controls for human review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI-enabled tools throughout product development and help establish effective practices for AI-assisted discovery, prototyping, specification, testing, and iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance new product development with reliability, operational ownership, and the long-term health of the portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management or equivalent experience leading the development of complex software products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience independently taking a product from problem discovery through launch, adoption, measurement, and iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with engineering and data teams on systems involving data models, integrations, APIs, or complex operational workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to synthesize the needs of multiple user groups and lead decisions across organizational boundaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate clearly about product strategy, priorities, tradeoffs, risks, and results with both technical and nontechnical partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building products for tax, treasury, accounting, regulatory reporting, or other control-sensitive domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with enterprise data platforms, workflow systems, internal tool development, or systems of record&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying AI or automation to expert workflows while preserving human review, auditability, and accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience maturing a product from active development into a reliable, sustainable operating model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Us&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we are on a mission to help build a better Internet. Today the company runs one of the world’s largest networks that powers millions of websites and other Internet properties for customers ranging from individual bloggers to SMBs to Fortune 500 companies. Cloudflare protects and accelerates any Internet application online without adding hardware, installing software, or changing a line of code. Internet properties powered by Cloudflare all have web traffic routed through its intelligent global network, which gets smarter with every request. As a result, they see significant improvement in performance and a decrease in spam and other attacks. Cloudflare was named to Entrepreneur Magazine’s Top Company Cultures list and ranked among the World’s Most Innovative Companies by Fast Company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we’re not looking for people who wait for a polished roadmap; we’re looking for the builders who see the cracks in the Internet that everyone else has simply learned to live with. We value candidates who have the instinct to spot a &quot;normalized&quot; problem and the AI-native curiosity to create a solution using the latest tools. Our culture is built on iteration, leveraging AI to ship faster today to make it better tomorrow, while ensuring that every improvement, no matter how small, is shared across the team to lift everyone up. If you’re the type of person who values curiosity over bureaucracy, and that AI is a partner in solving tough problems to keep the Internet moving forward, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Locations: Austin, San Francisco, or NYC&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cloudflare&#39;s developer platform lets developers build full-stack applications that run on a global network. Alongside Workers, developers rely on a growing set of data products: D1 for serverless SQLite, Durable Objects for stateful coordination, KV for global key-value storage, R2 for object storage, and Hyperdrive for connecting to existing databases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be leading a new database product from its earliest days. You will define what the product is, who it is for, and why developers should choose it over the databases they already know. Then you will get it to first customers and see it through to general availability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your mission in this role is to lead the project of building a database designed for agent-driven development workflows, getting both the core tradeoffs and the fine-grained details right.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run customer discovery to find and sharpen the problem the product should solve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the product, its target users, and its positioning against established databases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with engineering on core design tradeoffs across consistency, latency, scale, durability, and cost to serve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit design partners and run a private beta that produces honest, usable feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set success metrics and use them to decide what to build, change, or cut.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own pricing and packaging, grounded in customer value and unit economics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the product from first prototype through beta, launch, and GA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure it fits naturally with Workers, Wrangler, and Cloudflare&#39;s existing data products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Product Marketing, Developer Relations, Sales, and Customer Support teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Cloudflare externally at conferences, community events, customer meetings, and developer-focused initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Examples of Desirable Skills, Knowledge, and Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience as an EM, PM or founder. You&#39;ve led teams to ship before and can point to impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking a product from 0 to 1. You are comfortable with ambiguity and can turn an open problem into a clear plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real experience building on databases. You have modeled data, written queries, and run SQL or NoSQL databases in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid grasp of distributed-systems tradeoffs. You can reason through replication, consistency models, and failure modes with engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with pricing and unit economics for infrastructure. You know what a workload costs to serve and how that shapes a price.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep empathy for developers and how they choose and adopt new platforms. You understand what it&#39;s like to bet your application on a database someone else built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on ability to write code and use AI and the Internet to learn new things fast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and collaboration skills. You can translate between engineering domains and align diverse teams on goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for design details and polish. You raise the bar for sweating the details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;External presentation skills. You can walk into a room of developers and build trust and credibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compensation may be adjusted depending on work location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;For Seattle/NYC/California based hires - Estimated annual salary of: $172,000 - $215,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;For SF/Bay Area based hires - Estimated annual salary of: $179,000 - $224,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is eligible to participate in Cloudflare’s equity plan.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cloudflare offers a complete package of benefits and programs to support you and your family.&amp;nbsp; Our benefits programs can help you pay health care expenses, support caregiving, build capital for the future and make life a little easier and fun!&amp;nbsp; The below is a description of our benefits for employees in the United States, and benefits may vary for employees based outside the U.S.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health &amp;amp; Welfare Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical/Rx Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dental Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vision Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Spending Accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commuter Spending Accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fertility &amp;amp; Family Forming Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On-demand mental health support and Employee Assistance Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global Travel Medical Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Short and Long Term Disability Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life &amp;amp; Accident Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) Retirement Savings Plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Stock Participation Plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Time Off&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible paid time off covering vacation and sick leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leave programs, including parental, pregnancy health, medical, and bereavement leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;What Makes Cloudflare Special?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re not just a highly ambitious, large-scale technology company. We’re a highly ambitious, large-scale technology company with a soul. Fundamental to our mission to help build a better Internet is protecting the free and open Internet.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://blog.cloudflare.com/protecting-free-expression-online/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Galileo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;: Since 2014, we&#39;ve equipped more than 2,400 journalism and civil society organizations in 111 countries with powerful tools to defend themselves against attacks that would otherwise censor their work, technology already used by Cloudflare’s enterprise customers--at no cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cloudflare.com/athenian/&quot;&gt;Athenian Project&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;: In 2017, we created the Athenian Project to ensure that state and local governments have the highest level of protection and reliability for free, so that their constituents have access to election information and voter registration. Since the project, we&#39;ve provided services to more than 425 local government election websites in 33 states.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://1.1.1.1/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1.1.1.1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;: We released&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://1.1.1.1/&quot;&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;1.1.1.1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; to help fix the foundation of the Internet by building a faster, more secure and privacy-centric public DNS resolver. This is available publicly for everyone to use - it is the first consumer-focused service Cloudflare has ever released. Here’s the deal - we don’t store client IP addresses never, ever. We will continue to abide by our&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/1.1.1.1/privacy/public-dns-resolver&quot;&gt; privacy commitment&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; and ensure that no user data is sold to advertisers or used to target consumers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Sound like something you’d like to be a part of? We’d love to hear from you!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Please note that applicants who progress to the offer stage of the interview process may be asked to attend an in-person interview within one of the Cloudflare Offices or Cloudflare Hubs.&amp;nbsp; More details about this will be available at that stage of the interview process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This position may require access to information protected under U.S. export control laws, including the U.S. Export Administration Regulations. Please note that any offer of employment may be conditioned on your authorization to receive software or technology controlled under these U.S. export laws without sponsorship for an export license.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Cloudflare is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. &amp;nbsp;We are committed to providing equal employment opportunity for all people and place great value in both diversity and inclusiveness. &amp;nbsp;All qualified applicants will be considered for employment without regard to their, or any other person&#39;s, perceived or actual&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;race, color, religion, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, physical or mental disability, medical condition, family care status, or any other basis protected by law. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We are an AA/Veterans/Disabled Employer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Cloudflare provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. &amp;nbsp;Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job. Examples of reasonable accommodations include, but are not limited to, changing the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. &amp;nbsp;If you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job, please contact us via e-mail at &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;hr@cloudflare.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; or via mail at 101 Townsend St. San Francisco, CA 94107.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
